'''Silico''' ({{IPA-bl|siˈliko}}; {{Literal translation|{{W|silicon}}}}) is a [[Planned communities in Balisca|master-planned city]] in central [[Provence]], [[Cerdanya]], in the [[Rosario|Rosario metropolitan area]]. It was named in 1980 for the [[Silico Science and Industrial Park]] which it surrounds. The {{convert|36.4|km2|sqmi|adj=on}} city had a population of 225,872 at the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. As of 2025, it is the third-most populous city in Provence, fifth most in Cerdanya, and [[List of cities in Balisca by population|60th most in Balisca]].

A number of corporations, particularly in the technology and semiconductor sectors, have their national or international headquarters in Silico. Silico is also home to several higher-education institutions including the [[City University of Silico]] (CUSO), [[tba]], and [[tba]].

